Personas for docs/mid-drive-recovery-plan.md, as a patch to the end-to-end
harness at 191e15c. Apply it to a scratch copy, never to the tree:

    git archive 191e15c ios tools | tar -x -C <scratch>
    cd <scratch> && git apply <repo>/tools/mid_drive_personas.patch

It adds, to ios/Tests/SimulatedDrive*.swift:
- wrongWayAlong / loopWrongWay: a U-turn on the route itself, then up to 2 km
  back along the line, then round again (P-05);
- serverDown / loopServerDown: a missed turn onto a real road 1.5-3 km long,
  with every request failing for 180 s from the deviation (P-04);
- spike, canyon, loopMild, loopSpike, loopCanyon: re-created from the
  descriptions in the 2026-10-05 drive-simulation report;
- per-drive fields for each (rev*, outage*), and NavView.bannerText samples;
- six loops of 150-400 km in tools/e2e_od_pairs.json (longloop-*);
- ios/Tests/ReplayDumpTests.swift, which dumps every recorded drive's replay
  (arrival, fixes, replies, utterances) for a base-against-branch diff.

Run a persona with TEST_RUNNER_SUNDAYDRIVE_E2E=1, TEST_RUNNER_SUNDAYDRIVE_API
and -only-testing:SundayDriveTests/SimulatedDriveTests/test_12_wrongWayAlong
(test_12 to test_20; see the plan, section 11).

